    {
      "version": 1,
      "id": "mwjrn9r5zug49w",
      "title": "Tackling rolling donut - basic",
      "age": "U10",
      "category": "Contact",
      "length": 10,
      "width": 8,
      "objective": "Track a moving tackle donut, get balanced before contact, and finish a controlled tackle. The aim is good feet and a safe wrap, not a big hit.",
      "safety": "U10 supervised tackle practice. Use a properly padded donut and check the surface, space and equipment first. Start with slow, predictable rolls and only increase the challenge when each player can control their approach. Keep the waiting players and second coach outside the rolling/contact lane. Stop immediately for head-first contact, poor head position, loss of balance or an uncontrolled dive. Adults supervise and roll/reset the equipment; they are not the tackle target. No player-on-player contact or ruck follows this drill. Follow current RFU age-grade and club tackle guidance.",
      "frames": [
